# ---- Test-tree build artifacts (structural rule, not a name list) ----
#
# 2026-08-26: 566 build artifacts were TRACKED (~9 MB), so every `make check`
# dirtied them and `git status` was useless for reviewing a change. They are
# identified by CONTENT, not by name — verified before untracking: 558 are ELF
# executables, 4 are Windows .exe, and 4 are .c files whose first line reads
# "Generated by ZER compiler — do not edit". Two files in these trees that
# LOOK like artifacts are genuine sources and stay tracked:
# rust_tests/qemu/link.ld and rust_tests/qemu/startup.c.
#
# The rule below is structural: under a test tree, a file is a SOURCE only if
# it carries a source extension. That replaces the hand-maintained name list
# that used to live here, which is the same deny-list shape this project keeps
# replacing with gates — it silently missed every new test the moment one was
# added.
tests/zer/*
!tests/zer/*.zer
!tests/zer/*.h
tests/zer_fail/*
!tests/zer_fail/*.zer
tests/zer_trap/*
!tests/zer_trap/*.zer
tests/zer_proof/*
!tests/zer_proof/*.zer
tests/zer_gaps/*
!tests/zer_gaps/*.zer
rust_tests/*
!rust_tests/*.zer
!rust_tests/*.sh
!rust_tests/*.md
!rust_tests/qemu/
zig_tests/*
!zig_tests/*.zer
!zig_tests/*.sh
!zig_tests/*.md
test_modules/*
!test_modules/*.zer
!test_modules/*.sh
!test_modules/*.md

